{# ============================================================
   EXHIBIT NHBE-c  |  Defence Case File
   ============================================================ #}

{% set gridded = "<strong>NHBE-c-gridded</strong>" %}

<div class="exhibit-wrapper">

  {# ── EXHIBIT HEADER ─────────────────────────────────────── #}
  {{ exhibit_header([
      [["Exhibit Reference", "NHBE-c"],       ["Associated Gridded Reference", "NHBE-c-gridded"]],
      [["Subject Property",  FF],             ["Claimant / Neighbouring Holding", FFH]],
  ]) }}


  {# ── IMAGE OVERVIEW ─────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <div class="section">
    <h3>Image Overview</h3>

    {{ rotate_90 }}

    <p>
      An image taken pointing in an approximately westerly direction.
      The right-hand side of the image in the lower quarter shows a portion of
      the access track over which {{ FFH }} enjoys a right of way.
      The left-hand side of the lower quarter depicts a concrete yard forming
      part of {{ FF }}; the yard has a large amount of tall grass growing around
      it and at some places on it, which from the given angle prevents viewing
      of the actual concrete that forms the basis of the yard.
    </p>
    <p>
      For clarity, grid references as displayed on {{gridded}} may be used
      when identifying the items described below.
    </p>
  </div>

  {# ── EXHIBIT ITEMS ───────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <div class="exhibit-items-row">

    {# ── ITEM 1 — BURGUNDY VAN ───────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="section exhibit-item">
      <h3>Item 1 &mdash; Burgundy Van</h3>

      <table class="item-meta" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3" border="1">
        <tr>
          <td width="30%"><strong>Grid Reference ({{gridded}})</strong></td>
          <td><i>I6</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Location in Image</strong></td>
          <td>Far extent of the view along the track</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <table class="item-section">
        <tr><th>Description</th></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <p>
            A burgundy van-type vehicle (exact make and model unclear) is parked at the
            far extent of the view along the track. The vehicle is presumably operated
            by an actor working on behalf of {{ NHB }} in some capacity unknown.
          </p>
        </td></tr>
      </table>

      <table class="item-section">
        <tr><th>Defence Response to Claims Made</th></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <strong>Obstruction and nuisance:</strong>
              Following the strict interpretation laid down by {{ NHB }}, this vehicle
              is causing an obstruction and a nuisance by parking on the right of way
              instead of using it for its intended purpose to pass and re-pass.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    {# ── ITEM 2 — IBC CONTAINER ──────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="section exhibit-item">
      <h3>Item 2 &mdash; IBC Container</h3>

      <table class="item-meta" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3" border="1">
        <tr>
          <td width="30%"><strong>Grid Reference ({{gridded}})</strong></td>
          <td><i>{# TODO: confirm grid reference #}</i></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Location in Image</strong></td>
          <td>Approximately halfway down the image, one third in from the right, in the foreground</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <table class="item-section">
        <tr><th>Description</th></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <p>
            An IBC container is positioned set back from the access track in a manner
            that prevents vehicles from entering onto the yard, as is common practice.
            IBC containers consist of smooth rounded injection-moulded seamless metallic
            caging and are not seemingly an immediate hazard to anyone.
            Their construction incorporates the following characteristics:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>eliminates rust and sharps throughout service life;</li>
            <li>spot-welded construction eliminates weaknesses, sharps, and failures associated with bolts;</li>
            <li>round corners to all extrusions in fabrication to eliminate sharp corners;</li>
            <li>impact-resistant design to accommodate impact without creating sharps and laceration injury.</li>
          </ul>
          {# Picture Required #}
        </td></tr>
      </table>

      <table class="item-section">
        <tr><th>Defence Response to Claims Made</th></tr>
        <tr><td>
          <ol>
            <li>
              <strong>Infringement upon public access:</strong>
              The IBC is positioned in from the access track in a way as to prevent
              vehicles from entering onto the yard, as is common practice. The exhibit
              does not identify an IBC container that could be considered to infringe
              upon the farm track.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Nuisance:</strong>
              It is unclear in what capacity the IBC is a nuisance.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Waste material:</strong>
              It is unclear how a usable, undamaged container on a concrete yard
              constitutes waste material.
            </li>
          </ol>
          {# TODO: flesh out Item 2 defence with further reasoning #}
        </td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    {# ── ITEM 3 — WHITE MERCEDES SPRINTER VAN ────────────────── #}
    <div class="section exhibit-item">
      <h3>Item 3 &mdash; White Mercedes Sprinter Van</h3>

      <table class="item-meta" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3" border="1">
        <tr>
          <td width="30%"><strong>Grid Reference ({{gridded}})</strong></td>
